  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nDetecting environment such as worker, worklet is rather difficult currently. There is no standard way to know what the execution environment is.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nWe can rely on the existence of the ```window``` object for the main thread, or the existence of ```importScript``` for workers, ... There are so many ways, but they are complicated and unreliable.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nI would have a global ```ENVRONMENT``` string that evaluate to the current environment, so that we can check via something like ```if(ENVIRONMENT === \"worker\")```. There would be one for worker (possibly dedicated and shared), audio worklet, shared storage worklet, animation worklet,...\n\n### Anything else?\n\nThere are use cases where this can help, such as inlining web workers and audioworklet. We can ```new Worker()```, ```audioCtx.addModule()``` all using one file. We can create the script that checks the current environment, like so:\r\n```\r\nswitch(ENVIRONMENT) {\r\n  case \"main_thread\":\r\n    // Run main thread code\r\n  case \"worker\":\r\n    // Run worker code\r\n  case \"audioWorklet\":\r\n    // Run audioWorklet\r\n}\r\n```",
